  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0061","idiomatic","Zhilugu, Wang Bai, and Yelü Diru committed no great wrongs or merits — it is right that they be recorded.","Zhilugu, Wang Bai, and Yelü Diru had neither great merits nor demerits — it is right that they be recorded.","無大得失 means they had no great merits or demerits (gains or losses); 'committed no great wrongs or merits' misrenders 得失 and pairs 'committed' with merits unnaturally. The proposed 'neither great merits nor demerits' matches the Chinese and is natural English.","high","applied"]
